{"title":"Idempotence","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is idempotent if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3b8f3377d3bef164b2bc5c226e2108c66bd1613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=f(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Idempotence&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Any constant function is idempotent.</li>\n<li>The function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/4874544e2638f3712dbb70e5ccf37558a5fc0acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> is idempotent.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Signum_function\" title=\"Signum function\">signum function</a> is idempotent.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Absolute_value\" title=\"Absolute value\">absolute value</a> function is idempotent.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greatest_integer_function\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Greatest integer function\">greatest integer function</a> is idempotent, as is the least integer function.</li>\n<li>Unions and intersections are idempotent, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42adead574bf32b6f2bb410cba28c3456bf8f0a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\cup A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17d27e9c6f57c017b9fd915cbd66f178bd771b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\cap A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> are both equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Idempotence&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018090912\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 31/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1057/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.058      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.058      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7289:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018090912 and revision id 240112. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}